           9950928430b8ea042f8184d8a5b8ed644c69a81cb9808d38e1525a506bf84460.

catalog.json
  The categories (Dynamic Wallpapers, Gradients), the default wallpaper (solar-gradients) and twelve
  solid colours.

oxyos/light.svg, oxyos/dark.svg (OxyOS, following the appearance)
  Two silk ribbons crossing a field of OxyOS's blue, lit from the upper right.

horizon/{night,dawn,sunrise,morning,day,afternoon,sunset,dusk}.svg (Horizon: following the sun)
  A sky over three ridges at eight moments of the day, each tagged with the sun's elevation and
  azimuth it shows (docs/adr/0012-solar-wallpaper.mdx); the night's and dusk's and dawn's stars
  are 140 seeded points.

{ocean,iris,orchid,coral,ember,meadow,lagoon,graphite}/{light,dark}.svg (Gradients, following
the appearance)
  The OxyOS wallpaper's silk in each of Bloom's accent hues (graphite: nearly without hue).

solar-gradients/*.jpg and solar-gradients/wallpaper.json (Solar Gradients: the default, following
the sun through sixteen variants, docs/adr/0012-solar-wallpaper.mdx)
  An original procedural work of OxyOS, made on 8 November 2026. Each variant is rendered, at
  6144 x 3456, by crates/oxyos-wallpaper/examples/make-solar-gradients.rs from the parameters in
  scripts/solar-gradients.json and nothing else: two radial gradients summed in OKLab (one centred
  a picture's height above its top, one stretched six times across below its bottom edge), each a
  Catmull-Rom curve through ten and seven colour stops, turned into sRGB, dithered with triangular
  noise of one level from a hash of the pixel, and written as JPEG (quality 92, 4:4:4). The look
  was matched, at the owner's request, to Apple's macOS wallpaper of the same name: its stops'
  colours and positions and each variant's sun were measured from a copy of it used only as a
  reference. No pixel of Apple's picture is embedded, resampled or traced; what is shipped is the
  renderer's output from those numbers.
